{
  "rationale": "Model sensing and actuation as simple plants, then encode the exploration policy in compact deterministic specifications. The policy keeps clear-space behavior strongly forward-biased, uses short directed turns for side obstacles, uses a rare one-shot backward escape only for front blockage, and reserves full_rotate for a dedicated repeated-failure last-resort path. Action states are one-shot in the specifications, while uncontrollable events are total in every specification state.",
  "strategy": [
    "Use separate plants for sensor outcomes and motion capabilities so the supervisor can compose perception with action constraints cleanly.",
    "Use one main policy specification plus a small progress-favoring specification to prefer move_forward over random_walk in normal clear operation while still allowing random_walk only in a dedicated clear-search helper state."
  ],
